Here's an example of how you can achieve this:

1. Add the following code to your `location /` block:
```nginx
location / {
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    index index.html index.htm;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;

    # Add this code to add a link to every post
    set $post_id "";
    rewrite ^/([0-9]+)/? permanent;
    set $post_id $1;

    if ($post_id != "") {
        set $post_link "/post/$post_id";
    }
}
```
This code uses the `rewrite` directive to capture the post ID from the URL and store it in the `$post_id` variable. It then sets the `$post_link` variable to the URL of the post.

2. Modify your HTML template to include the link. You can add the following code to your `index.html` file:
```html
